SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Decisions That Changed the World
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192746\n\n5
 :30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion \nAs the United States celebrates its
  250th anniversary\, join us for a timely conversation examining the decis
 ions that have shaped America's role in the world. Drawing on a landmark 2
 026 survey conducted by the Council on Foreign Relations and the Society f
 or Historians of American Foreign Relations\, James M. Lindsay\, distingui
 shed senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations\, will be joined by
  Mary Yntema\, past President & CEO of WorldBoston\, a World Affairs Counc
 il\, and governance and strategy consultant\, to explore the ten most cons
 equential successes—and failures—in U.S. foreign policy since the nati
 on's founding.\n\nThrough the lenses of history\, strategy\, and democrati
 c values\, this discussion will consider what these pivotal choices reveal
  about American leadership\, global engagement\, and the challenges that l
 ie ahead. At a moment when the international order is once again being red
 efined\, this promises to be a thought-provoking exploration of how the pa
 st informs the future.\n\nMembers will also receive a copy of the survey's
  foreign policy scorecard\, providing an opportunity to weigh in on the ra
 nkings and continue the conversation with fellow attendees following the d
 iscussion.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members\, plus
  one guest. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
